    <string name="bike_about_origin">YABA was built in Frankfurt am Main for one second-hand S3 and for every bike that should keep riding. It has been tested with S3 firmware\u00A01.9.3.</string>
    <string name="bike_outbursts_title">Dutch curses</string>
    <string name="bike_outbursts_caption">Now and then YABA curses in Dutch, on the dot matrix here in the app, never while you ride. YABA cannot write to the bike’s own display.</string>
    <string name="bike_outbursts_list_title">The words</string>
    <string name="bike_outbursts_list_hint">Press and hold a word to see it on the matrix.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_balen">Literally: to be annoyed. Meant: what a pity.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_gedoe">Literally: fuss. Meant: trouble, bother.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_nou_ja">Literally: well, yes. Meant: oh well.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_he_he">Literally: at last. Meant: phew.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_auw">Literally: ouch. Meant: that hurt.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_verdorie">Literally: a softened form of “verdomme”. Meant: darn it.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_de_pijp_uit">Literally: out of the pipe. Meant: finished, over.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_bek_dicht">Literally: beak shut. Meant: quiet.</string>
    <string name="bike_outburst_meaning_verdomme">Literally: damn me. Meant: damn it. The bike never says it on its own.</string>
